# SHA-256 of words the public repository must never carry (lowercase, ASCII
# letters and digits): names of competing products and of third-party CAD
# programs, kept as hashes so that the list does not cite them either.
# tool/hooks/banned_names.dart checks the lines a commit adds against it and
# against the plain list in .git/info/banned-words (one word per line, local
# to a clone, never committed). Add a word: printf word | shasum -a 256
